## Purpose
Close #1256 without weakening Trusted Merge Control and unblock #1249/#1250, #1270 and staged #1269 continuous assurance.

## Root cause
Trusted validators under `scripts/kidults/portal/` execute the real canonical Portal runtime modules:
- `apps/kidults-enterprise-staging/public/portal-r001/projection-store.js`
- `apps/kidults-enterprise-staging/public/portal-r001/proof-product-admission.js`
- `apps/kidults-enterprise-staging/public/portal-r001/proof-product-schema-validator.js`

The `pull_request_target` trust checker currently treats every executable dependency outside `scripts/` as an escape, while repository-local validation already depends on these exact canonical runtime modules. Copying/mirroring them or hiding execution behind a subprocess would create semantic drift or checker bypass and is prohibited.

## Proposed narrow migration
Define an explicit governed executable-root set containing:
1. existing trusted `scripts/` closure; and
2. ONLY the three exact canonical Portal runtime modules above, plus only their recursively resolved repository-local dependencies if independently enumerated and byte-bound.

Mandatory invariants:
- repository filesystem escape remains rejected;
- new executable dependency outside the enumerated governed roots remains rejected;
- transitive dependency closure is recursively resolved;
- baseline dependency bytes are immutable for ordinary PR merge-result comparison unless the PR explicitly changes the governed dependency and all affected controls run;
- additive validator/action/workflow injection remains rejected;
- action SHA/runtime/dependency locks remain required;
- no wildcard `apps/**` allowlist;
- no caller-controlled path or dynamic import expansion;
- adversarial tests must reject sibling app modules, parent traversal, symlink/path normalization escape, dynamic dependency injection and dependency removal/downgrade.

## Required proof before landing
- exact dependency graph receipt for the three Portal modules;
- mutation suite for escape/addition/removal/downgrade;
- Trusted Merge Control exact-head and merge-result SUCCESS;
- Full Value Chain aggregate SUCCESS;
- independent security review;
- #1250/#1270 merge-result reproof after migration.

## Authority boundary
THIS ISSUE DOES NOT AUTHORIZE THE TRUST-ROOT CHANGE. Because this changes `pull_request_target` trust semantics, explicit Program Owner/Security approval is required before implementation/landing. Until approved, checker bypass, broad allowlisting, mirrored runtime copies and trust downgrade are prohibited.

No provider/data/spend/credential/remote mutation/Public/Production/G5 effect. Empirical launch truth unchanged.
